Run, Dash!

208
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:22,640
Oh, yum, these are good! Good! Nice work!

209
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:25,520
That son of a bird is eating the biscuits!

210
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:26,740
It's crazy!

211
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:30,997
Why would you even think
to do that, you freak?

212
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:33,680
Because biscuits are food and I'm hungry!

213
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:34,797
That's right, Luffy!

214
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:37,977
And the best way to get rid
of food is to eat it all up!

215
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:39,840
So dig in and don't stop!

216
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:43,700
This Fraulein is tremendously crafty, ya!

217
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:11,820
This looks really bad.

218
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,473
Did they knock him out?

219
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:21,140
Get out of my way.

220
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:25,297
Lady Race, we were just
going to give him treatment.

221
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:28,260
I said, get out of my way! I'm sorry!

222
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,030
Pathetic.

223
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:39,742
Are you going to meet your
fiancé with that face?

224
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:44,805
All you had to do was
give up on that old chef.

225
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:47,509
Then you wouldn't have
to suffer like this.

226
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:50,360
Why did you come back?

227
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:54,100
It makes no sense.

228
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:57,680
You said that you wanted to
forget this place. Sanji.

229
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:22,297
I think I might actually be full now.

230
00:22:22,380 --> 00:22:23,580
You should be.

231
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:27,942
Hey, we've been at this forever.

232
00:22:28,140 --> 00:22:29,900
I'm so sick of fighting you.

233
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:34,340
You eat, you run away.

234
00:22:34,540 --> 00:22:36,422
You come back and eat some more.

235
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:40,620
Is this Straw Hat guy even human?

236
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:45,134
General Cracker may be scary, but that
guy's appetite is the real terror.

237
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:46,880
My General Cracker.

238
00:22:47,460 --> 00:22:51,300
So with his power, he really can
keep making biscuits forever?

239
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:53,137
Yeah.

240
00:22:53,220 --> 00:22:54,280
Just wait.

241
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:56,820
