I tell her about your untimely betrayal.

253
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:33,330
What?

254
00:23:33,413 --> 00:23:35,886
Shearing off mine branches
wasn't cool enough?

255
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:37,940
That's not fair, my general.

256
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,380
This Fraulein has Mama's Weaver card.

257
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:44,620
She's using us power to
make us bow down to her.

258
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:48,220
So technically it's Mama's
power we are obeying.

259
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:55,080
Save your excuses for her then Cause
I'll never forgive you bastards for this

260
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:59,457
This would be over if you
hadn't helped that insufferable

261
00:23:59,540 --> 00:24:02,697
woman My biscuit warriors
are supposed to be invincible

262
00:24:02,780 --> 00:24:05,757
And now look at them reduced
to yummy crunchy snacks all

263
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:10,500
thanks to you Stop your whining
This is a pirate battle, isn't it?

264
00:24:10,620 --> 00:24:12,717
So what if I figured out your weakness?

265
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:15,357
That doesn't mean you get to take
it out on my underlings, okay?

266
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:17,860
Ha-ha! Ha-ha! Underlings!

267
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:20,897
Is that really what we've been reduced to?

268
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:22,660
Is that a problem?

269
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:25,700
No, ma 'am! Sorry! Hmph!

270
00:24:26,140 --> 00:24:27,611
Let's put an end to this!

271
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:28,920
Biscuit warriors!

272
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:33,860
It's over, Straw Hat.

273
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:38,127
They come right back
when I break them apart.

274
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:40,237
So far, eating's all that's worked.

275
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:41,360
But, uh...

276
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:43,817
I'm not really hungry anymore.

277
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:47,000
Make sure to protect me, homies, or else!

278
00:24:47,340 --> 00:24:48,580
Yes, ma 'am!

279
00:24:48,780 --> 00:24:49,720
Hey, Nami!

280
00:24:50,260 --> 00:24:52,848
Can we try something
other than eating them?

281
00:24:53,940 --> 00:24:56,617
There's got to be a way to
stop them from reforming!

282
00:24:56,700 --> 00:24:57,641
Weather egg, go!

283
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:02,861
Your boss may be an emperor, but
I don't know you and I don't care!

284
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:07,157
Luffy won't lose, because he's
going to be king of the pirates!

285
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:10,140
In other words, there's
no limit to his appetite!

286
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:12,837
Come on!

287
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:18,060
I've been eating all night long still he
hungers, his stomach's like a black hole.

288
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:19,930
Please.

289
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:49,240
Oh, do it, Tanchi!

290
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:50,620
This is for you!

291
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:03,360
Oh, please don't let me!

292
00:26:11,540 --> 00:26:12,540
Lord Judge.

293
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:18,697
We're ready, all preparations are
complete here as well, good now.

294
00:26:18,780 --> 00:26:22,237
Inform my children—we're
departing for the whole cake Shit.

295
00:26:22,320 --> 00:26:27,457
Ready this'll hurt!

296
00:26:27,540 --> 00:26:28,897
Just put it on already.

297
00:26:28,980 --> 00:26:32,137
Barely tingles,

298
00:26:32,220 --> 00:26:33,577
the

299
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:40,660
swelling

300
00:26:42,180 --> 00:26:49,180
has

301
00:26:50,120 --> 00:26:50,950
gone

302
00:26:51,033 --> 00:26:51,863
down.

303
00:26:51,946 --> 00:26:54,597
Swelling is the only thing the mask fixes;

304
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:57,657
it suppresses the body's
natural response to

305
00:26:57,740 --> 00:27:00,377
an injury but it actually
slows your recovery.

306
00:27:00,460 --> 00:27:01,290
It's

307
00:27:01,420 --> 00:27:04,437
better than showing a face like
that to your fiancee though.

308
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:08,917
The charlotte family never
takes their spouse's last name.

309
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:12,057
You won't be a vinsmoke anymore if you get

310
00:27:12,140 --> 00:27:13,677
along well enough—you
might live a happy life.

311
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:14,590
Shut up!

312
00:27:14,673 --> 00:27:18,617
I don't know what you're
expecting from me.

313
00:27:18,700 --> 00:27:20,737
You came here on your own.

314
00:27:20,820 --> 00:27:21,650
your own

315
00:27:28,060 --> 00:27:29,300
Here's a question.

316
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:32,240
Where did that chivalry come from?

317
00:27:39,480 --> 00:27:42,540
Women! Women! Women! Women! Women!

318
00:27:45,140 --> 00:27:46,480
Not a chance!

319
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:48,860
I am not hiring any ladies here!

320
00:27:50,580 --> 00:27:52,360
Shut the hell up!

321
00:27:55,420 --> 00:27:59,640
You know I punctuate my lessons
with a swift kick to the face.

322
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:02,420
I can't very well treat a woman that way.

323
00:28:02,860 --> 00:28:03,960
And why not?

324
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:07,077
If you can kick me, then
you can kick a girl, too.

325
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:08,300
You little fool!

326
00:28:12,660 --> 00:28:14,020
What did I say?

327
00:28:14,780 --> 00:28:15,610
Listen up!

328
00:28:15,740 --> 00:28:17,700
A man must never kick a lady.

329
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:21,077
That's been the golden rule
since the age of the dinosaurs.

330
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:22,219
You understand me?

331
00:28:23,080 --> 00:28:24,940
All right, here's the deal.

332
00:28:25,280 --> 00:28:27,497
As a human, you're gonna make mistakes.

333
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:28,497
That's only natural.

334
00:28:28,580 --> 00:28:31,940
But as a man, if you ever
stray from the honorable path,

335
00:28:32,140 --> 00:28:34,297
then I'll chop off your
balls as punishment!

336
00:28:34,380 --> 00:28:37,040
and slit my own throat
while I'm at it. What?

337
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:39,619
Why would you slit your own throat?

338
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:46,740
Because as a parent, I gotta
take responsibility too.

339
00:28:48,140 --> 00:28:50,317
Don't become the kind of person I hate.

340
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,694
That's all I'm saying.

341
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:57,880
Now get back to work, why don't you?

342
00:29:02,120 --> 00:29:04,860
The Golden Rule from the Age of Dinosaurs.

343
00:29:05,420 --> 00:29:06,250
Huh?

344
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:15,980
May I enter, please?

345
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:20,737
Sanji, sir, it's time to depart.

346
00:29:20,820 --> 00:29:24,820
You have an engagement ceremony
to attend at the Whole Cake Shit.

347
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:33,833
Here, you'd better put on a clean shirt.

348
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:36,337
You're a member of the
royal family after all.

349
00:29:36,420 --> 00:29:40,126
You need to present yourself like
a Vinsmoke or we'll look bad.

350
00:29:40,300 --> 00:29:41,600
Like I give a crap.

351
00:29:52,720 --> 00:29:55,820
Meanwhile, in Brule's mirror world...

352
00:29:56,740 --> 00:29:59,040
Looks like I found you!

353
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:03,360
You found me!

354
00:30:07,140 --> 00:30:08,940
You'll never escape me!

355
00:30:17,820 --> 00:30:20,600
I don't think I can run anymore, Chumper!

356
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:26,744
If you trip and break a mirror,
your luck's gonna get even worse.

357
00:30:33,520 --> 00:30:35,540
Have a wonderful wedding!

358
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:41,460
Good luck, Sanji, sir!

359
00:30:42,780 --> 00:30:43,610
Congratulations!

360
00:30:43,693 --> 00:30:44,523
Congratulations!

361
00:30:47,900 --> 00:30:52,040
And so begins a new era
for the Vinsmoke family.

362
00:31:03,060 --> 00:31:04,260
Sanji, sir!

363
00:31:04,920 --> 00:31:08,180
Wave to the citizens now, Sanji. Go on.

364
00:31:24,440 --> 00:31:25,840
All right, guys!

365
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:27,260
Set sail!

366
00:31:48,100 --> 00:31:50,120
Enough is enough, you bastards!

367
00:31:50,620 --> 00:31:53,200
No more biscuits, everybody go home, OK?

368
00:31:55,420 --> 00:31:57,940
So you're finally full. I'm full,

369
00:31:58,040 --> 00:32:02,922
but I'm holding all those biscuits I ate
in my stomach if it's the last thing I do.

370
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:08,412
I don't need you to throw up to win this.

371
00:32:08,600 --> 00:32:10,640
I'll just pop you right open.

372
00:32:11,580 --> 00:32:12,920
Careful, Loopy!

373
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:15,600
Joke's on you!

374
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:17,073
I'm stuffed with power!

375
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:18,760
Muscle Balloon!

376
00:32:41,980 --> 00:32:44,080
What the hell?!

377
00:33:04,640 --> 00:33:05,840
Fourth gear, go!

378
00:33:12,620 --> 00:33:16,780
I call this form Tank
Man Stuffed Vergeing!

379
00:33:19,460 --> 00:33:21,180
Oh wow, he's huge!

380
00:33:28,140 --> 00:33:31,777
That's got kind of a different
feel than your last transformation,

381
00:33:31,860 --> 00:33:35,720
but can you even move because
you look pretty bloated to me?

382
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:44,380
General Cracker's blade can't cut out!

383
00:33:44,580 --> 00:33:46,280
What's this guy made out of?

384
00:33:47,980 --> 00:33:51,760
I've had enough of you,
you stubborn little pest.

385
00:33:55,420 --> 00:33:58,240
You've pushed me over the edge, Stryhat.

386
00:33:58,580 --> 00:33:59,420
It's over.

387
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:00,820
Time to die!

388
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:06,040
If I can't cut you, then
I'll stab you instead! Honey!

389
00:34:08,160 --> 00:34:08,990
Brunzo!

390
00:34:13,740 --> 00:34:14,760
One more!

391
00:34:15,100 --> 00:34:17,900
I'll burst you open this
time, mark my words!

392
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:22,760
Crash pretzel!

393
00:34:32,660 --> 00:34:34,020
Lupi, are you okay?

394
00:34:41,620 --> 00:34:43,020
Uh, uh, what?

395
00:34:43,200 --> 00:34:45,376
His skin is hard, but it's soft, too?

396
00:34:48,140 --> 00:34:48,970
Damn it!

397
00:34:49,100 --> 00:34:50,840
I can't pull away!

398
00:34:54,020 --> 00:34:55,060
Biscuit warriors!

399
00:34:56,760 --> 00:34:57,740
Rain Spark!

400
00:34:58,560 --> 00:34:59,390
Nami!

401
00:34:59,473 --> 00:35:00,517
Don't get the biscuits wet!

402
00:35:00,600 --> 00:35:02,217
I have a different plan this time!

403
00:35:02,300 --> 00:35:04,006
And I need them to stay hard!

404
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:17,760
Look! I can't move!

405
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:19,500
What's he trying to do?

406
00:35:19,740 --> 00:35:22,960
I'm gonna show you the power
of me on a full stomach!

407
00:35:23,820 --> 00:35:25,680
Time for you to fly!

408
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:44,360
I'll send you to the far
ends of the new world!

409
00:35:44,900 --> 00:35:46,920
Dog-gog cannonball!

410
00:35:48,900 --> 00:35:50,840
No more biscuits!

411
00:36:15,060 --> 00:36:16,280
Oh, my God.
